---
import { Picture } from 'astro:assets';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CallToAction from '../../components/CallToAction.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/PageHero.astro';
import riverPhoto from '../../assets/communities/wichita/wichita-river-sunset-kansastourism-Jason Lindsey.jpg';
import keeperPhoto from '../../assets/communities/wichita/wichita-keeper-of-the-plains-kansastourism-NoC.jpg';
import ballparkPhoto from '../../assets/communities/wichita/wichita-wind-surge-wide-kansastourism-Ed Bailey Photography 2020.jpg';
import explorationPhoto from '../../assets/communities/wichita/wichita-exploration-place-kansastourism-2016 Ryan Donnell.jpg';
import zooPhoto from '../../assets/communities/wichita/wichita-sedgwick-county-zoo-kansastourism-2016 Ryan Donnell.jpg';
import riverfestPhoto from '../../assets/communities/wichita/wichita-riverfest-river-kansastourism-NoC.jpg';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Wichita, Kansas Community Guide | Charity Menefee"
  description="A grounded introduction to Wichita, Kansas, covering how the city is organized, its riverfront and landmarks, and practical real estate guidance from Charity Menefee."
  pageClass="page-interior page-wichita"
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Community guide · Wichita"
    title="A city with many ways to feel at home."
    intro="Wichita brings together established neighborhoods, newer residential areas, a recognizable riverfront, and the everyday conveniences of the region's largest city."
    image={riverPhoto}
    imageAlt="The downtown Wichita skyline reflected in the Arkansas River at dusk, with a full moon rising"
    variant="community"
    imagePosition="center 58%"
    imagePositionMobile="58% 55%"
    photoCredit="© Jason Lindsey"
  />

  <section class="section-space" aria-labelledby="wichita-overview-title">
    <div class="shell editorial-grid">
      <div data-reveal="left"><p class="eyebrow">Getting oriented</p><h2 id="wichita-overview-title">One city, a wide range of settings.</h2></div>
      <div class="prose" data-reveal="right">
        <p>Wichita sits at the heart of south-central Kansas. It covers a lot of ground, and the homes can look very different depending on where you're looking. You'll find older central neighborhoods, newer construction toward the edges of town, and plenty in between. Major roads like Kellogg, I-135, I-235, and K-96 help divide the city into areas that are easier to compare.</p>
        <p>The Arkansas River runs through the middle of it, and a lot of what people picture when they think of Wichita sits along that corridor. It's a useful reference point when you're trying to place a neighborhood.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="photo-story section-space section-surface" aria-labelledby="wichita-place-title">
    <div class="shell photo-story-grid">
      <div class="photo-story-copy" data-reveal="left">
        <p class="eyebrow">A sense of place</p>
        <h2 id="wichita-place-title">The Keeper anchors Wichita's riverfront.</h2>
        <p>The Keeper of the Plains stands at the confluence of the Big and Little Arkansas rivers, where two pedestrian suspension bridges meet the promontory it sits on. The 44-foot steel sculpture is the work of Blackbear Bosin, a Kiowa-Comanche artist from Wichita, and it was installed in 1974.</p>
        <p>It's the image most people carry of the city, and the plaza around it is a straightforward place to get your bearings. The riverfront path running from here is one of the easier ways to understand how the central neighborhoods sit relative to downtown.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="photo-story-main photo-story-keeper" data-reveal="right">
        <Picture src={keeperPhoto} formats={['avif', 'webp']} widths={[480, 720, 960, 1280, 1600]} sizes="(min-width: 48rem) 62vw, 100vw" alt="The Keeper of the Plains sculpture on its promontory beside a cable-stayed pedestrian bridge over the Arkansas River" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="photo-banner photo-banner-panorama section-surface" aria-labelledby="wichita-ballpark-title">
    <div class="photo-banner-media">
      <Picture
        src={ballparkPhoto}
        formats={['avif', 'webp']}
        widths={[960, 1440, 1920, 2560, 3200]}
        sizes="100vw"
        alt="A panoramic view across a full ballpark toward the Wichita skyline, with both teams lined up along the baselines"
      />
      <p class="photo-credit">© Ed Bailey Photography 2020</p>
    </div>
    <div class="shell photo-banner-copy" data-reveal="up">
      <p class="eyebrow">Along the west bank</p>
      <h2 id="wichita-ballpark-title">A ballpark put new attention on the Delano side of the river.</h2>
      <p>The Wichita Wind Surge, a Double-A affiliate of the Minnesota Twins, play on the west bank of the Arkansas River across from downtown, on the site where Lawrence-Dumont Stadium stood for decades. The ballpark opened in 2021 and was renamed Equity Bank Park in 2025.</p>
      <p>It sits at the edge of Delano, one of Wichita's older districts, and the surrounding blocks have drawn steady redevelopment interest. If you're looking at property on that side of the river, it's worth understanding how that area has been changing.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-space" aria-labelledby="wichita-attractions-title">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-heading split-heading">
        <div data-reveal="left">
          <p class="eyebrow">What's nearby</p>
          <h2 id="wichita-attractions-title">Two of the state's most-visited places are here.</h2>
        </div>
        <p data-reveal="right">Both sit on the west side of the city, within a few minutes of each other.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card-grid reveal-stagger">
        <figure class="feature-card" data-reveal="left-scale">
          <div class="feature-card-media">
            <Picture src={zooPhoto} formats={['avif', 'webp']} widths={[480, 720, 960, 1280]} sizes="(min-width: 48rem) 50vw, 100vw" alt="Visitors at a railing watching an elephant walk beside a stream in a large open habitat at the Sedgwick County Zoo" />
            <p class="photo-credit">© 2016 Ryan Donnell</p>
          </div>
          <figcaption>
            <strong>Sedgwick County Zoo</strong>
            <span>Opened in 1971 and now spread across 247 acres with roughly 400 species. It's AZA-accredited and the most-visited outdoor attraction in Kansas.</span>
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="feature-card" data-reveal="right-scale">
          <div class="feature-card-media wichita-attraction-exploration">
            <Picture src={explorationPhoto} formats={['avif', 'webp']} widths={[480, 720, 960, 1280]} sizes="(min-width: 48rem) 50vw, 100vw" alt="The concrete forms of Exploration Place beside the Arkansas River, with a footbridge leading to the entrance" />
            <p class="photo-credit">© 2016 Ryan Donnell</p>
          </div>
          <figcaption>
            <strong>Exploration Place</strong>
            <span>A science center on the river north of downtown, open since 2000. The building and its grounds were designed by architect Moshe Safdie.</span>
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="photo-story section-space section-sage" aria-labelledby="wichita-riverfest-title">
    <div class="shell photo-story-grid photo-story-reverse">
      <div class="photo-story-copy wichita-riverfest-copy" data-reveal="right">
        <p class="eyebrow">A yearly tradition</p>
        <h2 id="wichita-riverfest-title">Riverfest turns the riverbanks into the center of town.</h2>
        <p>Wichita Riverfest traces back to 1970 and runs for nine days each spring along the Arkansas River downtown. Concerts, fireworks, food vendors, and a set of long-running traditions draw crowds from across the region, and it's generally described as the largest community event in Kansas.</p>
        <p>It's a good illustration of how much of Wichita's public life is organized around the river, which is worth keeping in mind when you're weighing a central or riverside address against something farther out.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="photo-story-main photo-story-riverfest" data-reveal="left">
        <Picture src={riverfestPhoto} formats={['avif', 'webp']} widths={[480, 720, 960, 1080]} sizes="(min-width: 48rem) 42vw, 100vw" alt="Crowds lining the bank of the Arkansas River at night during Wichita Riverfest, with the lit downtown skyline behind them" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-space section-surface" aria-labelledby="wichita-growth-title">
    <div class="shell editorial-grid">
      <div data-reveal="left"><p class="eyebrow">Newer options</p><h2 id="wichita-growth-title">New homes are part of the picture.</h2></div>
      <div class="prose" data-reveal="right">
        <p>Residential additions such as Estancia, Southern Ridge, Brookfield, and Fontana illustrate how newer construction has appeared in several parts of Wichita. Those names are orientation points, not statements about current inventory or lot availability.</p>
        <p>If a newer home or building from the ground up is something you're considering, it's worth comparing the location, lot, builder, neighborhood plans, taxes, and long-term costs just as carefully as the house itself.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-space" aria-labelledby="wichita-search-title">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-heading split-heading"><div data-reveal="left"><p class="eyebrow">Planning a search</p><h2 id="wichita-search-title">Useful questions before choosing a part of town.</h2></div><p data-reveal="right">These are practical starting points, but they aren't a substitute for your own research or property-specific investigation.</p></div>
      <ul class="question-grid reveal-stagger">
        <li data-reveal="up">Which parts of Wichita fit the places you visit most often?</li>
        <li data-reveal="up">Do you prefer an older home, newer construction, or something in between?</li>
        <li data-reveal="up">How much yard and ongoing maintenance feel realistic?</li>
        <li data-reveal="up">Is the address in an established area, an infill setting, or a newer addition, and what does that mean for the lot and surrounding infrastructure?</li>
        <li data-reveal="up">If you're drawn to a riverside or central neighborhood, which flood-zone, lot, and older-home questions should be checked for that specific address?</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <nav class="shell next-community" aria-label="Community pages"><span>Next community</span><a href="/communities/valley-center/">Valley Center <i aria-hidden="true">→</i></a></nav>
  <CallToAction
    title="Thinking about a move within Wichita?"
    copy="If you're comparing communities or have questions about a specific property, tell me what you're considering. I’ll help you sort through the location and property details that matter."
  />
</BaseLayout>
